CORE dfcc-only
replacement.c
--dfcc main --replace-call-with-contract function/contract
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[caller\.precondition_instance\.1\] line 13 static array parameter .* must provide access to its declared minimum: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A source call replaced by a separately named contract still satisfies the
called function's C-level static minimum. The weaker contract's own
requires clause holds, and its generated specification functions add no
further static-array failure.
